    "resolved_from_fallback": false,
    "final_cot": "Image description: In the figure there are two intersecting line segments VX and ZY, and they intersect at point W. The left-side line segment VZ and the right-side line segment YX have the same arrow markings, indicating VZ ∥ YX. The figure is labeled VW = 3x - 6, WX = x + 4, ZW = 6, WY = 5. Reasoning: Because VZ ∥ YX, and the two oblique lines intersect at W, △VWZ and △XWY are similar. The corresponding sides are VW ↔ WX, ZW ↔ WY. Therefore there is the proportion (3x - 6)/(x + 4) = 6/5. Solve the equation: 5(3x - 6) = 6(x + 4), that is, 15x - 30 = 6x + 24, obtaining 9x = 54, so x = 6. Thus VW = 3x - 6 = 3(6) - 6 = 12.",
